image_cache: a temp name per process and thread for a badge download

download_static_image wrote <target>.tmp and renamed it into place. Two
workers fetching one asset -- the pool's four threads on a set whose
locked and unlocked badges share a file, or the service's pool and a bulk
cache's in another process (ROCKNIX runs one beside the service) -- both
passed the target.exists() test, both wrote the one .tmp, one's rename
moved the other's half-written bytes into place, and one's cleanup
unlinked the file the other was still writing (ROCKNIX audit #186 PL-33).

The temp name now carries the pid and the thread id, and the move is
os.replace, so the second writer to finish overwrites the first's
identical bytes instead of failing on an existing target. The duplicate
request itself remains -- a per-asset in-flight set is the next step and
is left to the project.

Written for ROCKNIX (fork issue maxengel/rocknix#186, PL-33). Offered
upstream as-is (ROCKNIX D-RA-016).

